<title>DUBAI: First tanker with Iraqi crude leaves Mina al-Bakr.</title>
<headline>First tanker with Iraqi crude leaves Mina al-Bakr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The VLCC Star of Africa left Iraq's Mina al-Bakr oil terminal in the northern Middle East Gulf late on Tuesday, a Gulf shipping source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tanker, which industry sources said had been chartered by U.S. firm Coastal Corp for delivery to its refinery on the Caribbean island of Aruba, is Iraq's first export from the Gulf for the first time since its 1990 invasion of Kuwait.</p>
<p>&quot;It left last night. The Leonidas is still loading,&quot; the shipping source said, referring to a second tanker at the terminal under charter from U.S. trader Bayoil.</p>
<p>The U.N. has approved seven contracts under the &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal with Baghdad.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
</text>
